<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Stun arcs pale blue: the Jawa ion signature (L4, L5, L16).

     WHAT THIS IS. The arcing electricity over a stunned pawn is vanilla's
     Mote_Stun (Core, Defs/Effects/Mote_MetaStatus.xml):

         <ThingDef ParentName="MoteBase">
           <defName>Mote_Stun</defName>
           <thingClass>MoteDualAttached</thingClass>
           <graphicData><texPath>Things/Mote/Stun</texPath></graphicData>
         </ThingDef>

     graphicData declares NO colour, so it draws untinted white. Adding one
     tints the mote, which is the whole change. Nothing else is touched: the
     texture, timing, altitude layer and thingClass are vanilla's.

     THE COLOUR is deliberately the same hue already used by JawaIon_Damage's
     explosionColorEdge (0.55, 0.75, 1.0) so a bolt's impact flash and the stun
     arc it leaves behind read as one effect rather than two.

     ⚠️ SCOPE: THIS IS GLOBAL, and that is a choice, not an oversight.
     Mote_Stun is Core and every stun in the game uses it. RimWorld spawns it
     from StunHandler against a hardcoded ThingDefOf.Mote_Stun, so there is no
     XML route to a per-source colour. Consequences worth accepting knowingly:

       * Jawa ion bolts arc pale blue. This is the point. JawaIon_Damage
         already sets causeStun true, so the effect is ours by default.
       * KotOR stun bolts, Outer Rim stun grenades and sonic weapons also arc
         pale blue. All energy weapons; consistent with the setting.
       * The Gamorrean Arg'garok arcs pale blue too, which is the one odd fit:
         it is an axe whose edge tool carries ExtraDamage Stun at chance 1.0.
         Living with it, because "electric shock looks like this here" is a
         coherent rule and a per-weapon exception is not worth C# for a tint.

     If ion-only colour is ever wanted, JawaIonWeapons already ships an
     assembly, so a Harmony postfix on the stun mote spawn is the route. It is
     not worth it for a tint today.

     Verified against the live dump 2026-08-11: Mote_Stun exists, is Core, and
     declares no colour. Conditional rather than Add so this cannot duplicate
     the node if Ludeon ever adds one. -->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Mote_Stun"]/graphicData/color</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Mote_Stun"]/graphicData/color</xpath>
      <value><color>(0.55, 0.78, 1.00, 1.00)</color></value>
    </match>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Mote_Stun"]/graphicData</xpath>
      <value><color>(0.55, 0.78, 1.00, 1.00)</color></value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
